            "target_entity_type": "Metric",
            "paragraph": "The second step of the GCM validation consisted in comparing the space distribution of seasonal mean averages of some selected fields with their observed counterparts. Two fields were chosen for this purpose, while being relevant in assessing the performance of a convection scheme. First, the zonal mean temperature was considered. This field provides a longitudinally integrated view of the temperature along the vertical, and thus gives an insight into the ability of the convection scheme to redistribute the heating in the vertical direction in the tropics. The reference used was the 44-yr reanalysis data set produced by ECMWF (ERA40, 1958 to 2001; Uppala et al., 2005), but limited to the years 1979-2001. Figure 13 illustrates the zonal mean temperature bias (GCM minus ERA40), for the four seasons. In the tropical tropospheric region, the bias is close to zero except around 30\u00b0, in the Hadley cell subsidence region, where it is slightly negative (maximum absolute bias of the order of 1 K, in the middle of the troposphere).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
